    "original_review_scope_verbatim": "Complete original Theorem5.1 and all defining autonomous-equation, n/y/bow-tie/genus-one/spectral-curve/outer-RH hypotheses and normalizations, with the full actual z-system derivation, algebraic matrix identity, squared scalar spectral identity and final first integral. The genuine new spectral-curve/g-function/lens-opening and outer-parametrix construction is retained, together with the full human-authored Boutroux/level-curve proof of Lemma2.1 in AppendixB. The theorem is the author-designated main goal: it identifies the equation satisfied by the defined RH outer approximation, including its integration constant. It does not claim a full asymptotic convergence theorem; the authors explicitly state that supplying all convergence details is outside this paper’s aim, and that scope is preserved. The optional toy-problem AppendixA is excluded, not mistaken for the real core proof. All four original figures and every literal formula/branch/citation remain unchanged. Standard RH, elliptic/quadratic-differential background stays as exact author references; no generated differential system or convergence proof is inserted.\n\nNo mathematical refereeing or assistant-generated proof. Native source and corresponding saved publisher PDF are hash-bound. Compiled in 3 fresh no-shell-escape passes, final actual log checked for stabilization and readable formula/matrix output compared with original pixels. See visual-qa.json and compile-evidence.json. Exact source archive binding and per-block byte verification passed. Full DOI verified on the saved publisher PDF first page.\n\nThe original panels illustrate contours/sign charts, with the required jump matrices and endpoint/orientation conditions fully editable in the native body and caption. No graphic matrix definition is used as a substitute for editable proof equations. Two harmless empty-anchor links retain visible original reference text; the optional illustrative Appendix A has an exact external locator.\n\n\nImmutable editorial revision r002: only the difficulty rationale in the attribution cover and metadata is replaced by the root-approved same-content two-sentence wording. Difficulty level, literal author body, excerpts, source/version/rights, figures and all mathematical assertions retain original bytes. Prior r001 packet and batch018 remain unchanged. Fresh stable compilation and cover/author-page visual comparison are recorded separately.\n",
